<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Tahiti</h1><p class="st-meta">1788 CE – 1880 CE · capital Papeete</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Polynesian kingdom built by the Pōmare dynasty with European guns and missionary support, which became a French protectorate and then a colony.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tahiti was divided among rival chiefdoms when European ships arrived from 1767. The chief Tu, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-i">Pōmare I</a>, used <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">muskets</a> obtained from visiting ships and the services of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hms-bounty">Bounty</a> mutineers to dominate the island from about 1788. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-ii">Pōmare II</a>, after defeat and exile on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moorea">Moorea</a>, won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fei-pi">Battle of Fei Pi</a> in 1815 and secured rule over Tahiti.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-ii">Pōmare II</a> converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a> and issued a written legal code in 1819. Protestant missionaries shaped law, schooling and the use of written Tahitian. The kingdom traded pork, coconut oil and pearl shell. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-iv">Queen Pōmare</a> IV, who reigned for fifty years, conflict between British Protestant missionaries and French Catholic priests drew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1842 Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abel-aubert-du-petit-thouars">Dupetit-Thouars</a> imposed a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-tahitian-war">Franco-Tahitian War</a> followed from 1844 to 1847. The protectorate was administered within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-establishments-in-oceania">French Establishments in Oceania</a>, and in 1880 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-v">Pōmare V</a> ceded the kingdom to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-tahiti.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Tahiti" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Vilallonga · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Tahiti.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1788 CE – 1880 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Papeete</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pōmare I, Pōmare II, Pōmare IV</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism, Polynesian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tahitian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tahiti, Pomare kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tahiti" aria-label="Kingdom of Tahiti on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="618 2829 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Tahiti lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M938 3085L5054 728M938 3085L938 3085"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M938 3085h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M938 3085h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M938 3085h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Papeete. <a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tahiti">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
